<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose four points to 1,264.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose four points to 1,264.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,264 today from 1,260 on May 2, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1354    12.293	  1358    12.331</p>
<p>   1a   1241  9400.000	  1234  9344.000</p>
<p>   2    1522    21.750	  1520    21.713</p>
<p>   2a   1481 12143.000	  1467 12031.000</p>
<p>   3    1365    12.593	  1360    12.550</p>
<p>   3a   1140  9000.000	  1132  8938.000</p>
<p>   6    1231    12.693	  1228    12.663</p>
<p>   7    1153     5.614	  1153     5.613</p>
<p>   8     884     9.721	   884     9.725</p>
<p>   9     697  6093.000	   692  6050.000</p>
<p>  10    1111     5.614	  1111     5.613</p>
